# 020 · A one-container rig image

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Rigs on RunPod · **Depends on:** [018](018-runpod-spike.goal)

## What

RunPod runs one container per pod. A combined rig image runs the broker as root and starts the supervisor under its own user, beside the role users. It removes every setuid and setgid bit at build time, and it keeps RunPod's own variables from every role. The isolation self-test checks all of this.

## Why

The harness and the supervisor normally run in two containers. RunPod allows one.

## Done when

- [ ] The combined image passes the isolation self-test on RunPod and in CI.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-20, owner: One combined image per pod, as recommended.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
- 2026-10-20: Built. `containers/rig/Containerfile` is the harness image (named in `HARNESS_IMAGE`; CUDA for pods, CPU for tests) with the supervisor's `openssh-client` and user added; its build removes every setuid and setgid bit and fails if one is left. Its entry point, `thermite-rig-start`, removes every `RUNPOD_` variable before `tini` starts, and passes the pod's ID on as `THERMITE_POD_ID`. With `THERMITE_ONE_CONTAINER=1` the broker (root) prepares the supervisor's places on the volume (`/workspace/thermite/...`), makes the harness token once, writes control's key from the launch, and starts the supervisor as uid 10001 with no_new_privs and in the GPU fence with no card. It restarts either part after an exit and ends both cleanly on a stop. No process it starts gets a `RUNPOD_` variable, in every image. The isolation selftest gains `pid1-environ` and `runpod-variables` probes for every role, the supervisor's places in this image, and container checks: the supervisor's user, its GPU access, set-id files and RunPod's variables. Docs: the image reference, the isolation explanation, rig checks, settings and contributing.
- 2026-10-20: Checks. Unit tests for the broker's parts, the entry point and the selftest's new checks. `scripts/rig-image-acceptance.mjs` passed under rootless Podman: the image started as RunPod starts it (root, default capabilities, no no-new-privileges, RunPod's eight variables made up), with GPU device nodes the container could not regroup (nobody's, 0666). The selftest passed, from the controller at start and as root; the fence alone kept the other roles and the supervisor off the nodes; a killed supervisor and a killed controller started again; a stop ended both with exit code 0 in 5 s. CI now runs the same script with Docker; it has not run there yet.
- 2026-10-20: For goals 019 and 021, the contract with this image: control's command-signing public key comes with the launch in `THERMITE_CONTROL_PUBKEY` (PEM, or PEM in base64); the broker writes it as root to `THERMITE_CONTROL_PUBKEY_FILE` (`/etc/thermite/control-signing.pub`), where both parts read it, and without it the harness waits without restarting. The supervisor's public port is `THERMITE_TUNNEL_PORT` (8000, `EXPOSE`d), the pod's ID is in `THERMITE_POD_ID`, and the supervisor's keys belong in `THERMITE_SUPERVISOR_HOME` (0700, its own). Nothing reads the port yet.
- 2026-10-20: Left: the selftest on RunPod, with the second spike run (goal 018, a paid launch that needs the owner's OK), and the first CI run.

